From: ThaRae <tharae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:13:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Give an endpoint its view while the page hosts
 its document

ScriptBridgeEndpoint::view_id() answered only for an endpoint whose
bridge was open, so the world-less endpoint of a web page, which never
has one, had no view. That is the endpoint a UserScriptHandler gets to
decide which scripts a document runs, and it has to know the view to
tell a private window's documents from the others.

Answer for any document the page still hosts.
---
 Libraries/LibWebView/URLSchemeHandler.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWebView/URLSchemeHandler.cpp b/Libraries/LibWebView/URLSchemeHandler.cpp
index e79a314514f1bec201ff33d6c86bc9c647ae1085..14dd2d0a9e024a17f2e4bafefe563d3dcda59bfc 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWebView/URLSchemeHandler.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWebView/URLSchemeHandler.cpp
@@ -79,9 +79,10 @@ bool ScriptBridgeEndpoint::is_open() const
 
 Optional<u64> ScriptBridgeEndpoint::view_id() const
 {
-    if (!is_open())
+    auto page = m_page.strong_ref();
+    if (!page || !page->hosted_document_endpoint(m_document_id).has_value())
         return {};
-    if (auto view = m_page->traversable().view(); view.has_value())
+    if (auto view = page->traversable().view(); view.has_value())
         return view->view_id();
     return {};
 }
